        "content": "Now let me solve the problem.\n\n**Solving:**\n\nFrom $f''_{yy}(x,y)=4$, integrate twice w.r.t. $y$:\n$$f'_y(x,y)=4y+\\varphi(x), \\quad f(x,y)=2y^2+y\\varphi(x)+\\psi(x)$$\n\nUse $f'_y(x,0)=\\sqrt2 x$: $f'_y(x,0)=\\varphi(x)=\\sqrt2 x$, so $\\varphi(x)=\\sqrt2 x$.\n\nUse $f(x,0)=x^2$: $f(x,0)=\\psi(x)=x^2$, so $\\psi(x)=x^2$.\n\nThus $f(x,y)=2y^2+\\sqrt2\\,xy+x^2$.\n\nOn $x^2+2y^2=4$, write $x=2\\cos t,\\ y=\\sqrt2\\sin t$:\n$$f=2\\cdot 2\\sin^2 t+\\sqrt2\\cdot 2\\cos t\\cdot\\sqrt2\\sin t+4\\cos^2 t = 4\\sin^2 t+4\\sin t\\cos t+4\\cos^2 t = 4+2\\sin 2t$$\n\nSo max $=6$, min $=2$.",
